metadata:
  name: Key Lime Pie
  images:
    - https://i.imgur.com/HvJ7UXb.png
  description: From https://www.onceuponachef.com/recipes/key-lime-pie.html 
  types: [Dessert]

ingredients:
 - 3.5 dl finely crushed graham cracker crumbs, from about 12 whole graham crackers
 - 0.75 dl packed light brown sugar
 - 4 tbsp unsalted butter, melted
 - 8 dl sweetened condensed milk
 - 2.36 dl Greek yogurt (2% or whole milk)
 - 1 tbsp grated lime zest
 - 1.75 dl fresh lime juice
 - 2.36 dl cold heavy cream
 - 2 tbsp confectioners' sugar
 - 1 tsp grated lime zest
 - 10 u thin lime slices

actions:
 - free_text Preheat oven to 190 C and set an oven rack in the middle position.
 - divider Make the crust
 - free_text In a medium bowl, combine 3.5 dl graham cracker crumbs, 0.75 dl packed light brown sugar, and 4 tbsp melted unsalted butter; stir with a fork first, and then your hands until the mixture is well combined.
 - free_text Using your fingers and the bottom of a measuring cup or glass, press the crumbs firmly into the bottom and up the sides of a 9-in deep-dish pie pan. The crust should be about 1/4-in thick. Do the sides first.
 - free_text Bake the crust for 10 minutes, or until lightly browned. Then let the crust cool a bit while you make the filling.
 - divider Make the filling
 - free_text Zest and juice the limes using a citrus reamer, then combine 1.75 dl juice and 1 tbsp zest with 8 dl sweetened condensed milk and 2.36 dl Greek yogurt. Whisk to combine.
 - free_text Pour the filling into the cooked graham cracker crust.
 - divider Bake the pie
 - free_text Bake for about 15 minutes, or until the filling is almost set.
 - free_text Let the pie cool at room temperature for 30 minutes, then place in the refrigerator to chill thoroughly, about 3 hours.
 - divider Make the topping
 - free_text In the bowl of an electric mixer fitted with the whisk attachment (or beaters), beat 2.36 dl cold heavy cream until soft peaks form. Add 2 tbsp confectioners’ sugar and beat until medium peaks form. (Alternatively, the cream can be beaten by hand with a whisk.)
 - free_text Top the chilled pie with whipped cream and decorate with 10 thin lime slices and 1 tsp grated lime zest.
